.UC 4
.SH NAME
sixel2png \- convert DEC SIXEL images into PNG format images


.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sixel2png
\fB-i\fP <input sixel file>
\fB-o\fP <output png file>
.br
.B img2sixel
\fB<\fP <input sixel file>
\fB>\fP <output png file>
.ta .5i 1.8i


.SH DESCRIPTION
.I sixel2png
convert DEC SIXEL images into PNG format images.
.PP
The converter accepts \(dqclipboard:\(dq as a pseudo file path for both input
and output.  Reading from \(dqclipboard:\(dq consumes the most recent SIXEL
image or UTF-8 string captured by the desktop clipboard.  Writing to
\(dqclipboard:\(dq publishes the decoded PNG bytes to the clipboard.  Combine
the pseudo target with format prefixes such as \(dqpng:clipboard:\(dq to select
a specific clipboard encoding.  Clipboard reads probe for PNG data first,
fall back to TIFF payloads, and finally attempt to decode UTF-8 strings.


.SH "COMMAND-LINE OPTIONS"
\fIsixel2png\fP has the following command-line options:
.TP 5
.B \-i
Specify input file. If it is omitted or "-",
this command accepts SIXEL data from STDIN.
.TP 5
.B \-o
Specify output file. If it is omitted or "-",
this command writes PNG data to STDOUT.  Prefixing the
argument with "png:" keeps the CLI consistent with img2sixel so
"png:-" maps to STDOUT and "png:\fIpath\fP" strips the prefix before
saving to disk.
.TP 5
.B \-d \fIMETHOD\fP, \-\-dequantize=\fIMETHOD\fP
Apply palette dequantization to the decoded image.
The argument specifies the method to use.
Unique prefixes are accepted.  The LSO undither modes also accept
"l:Vf" and "l:Vl" as compact aliases.
.RS
.TP 5
.B none
Disable dequantization (default).
.TP 5
.B k_undither
Use kornelski's undithering algorithm.
.TP 5
.B lso_undither:Vfs
Use the full Floyd-Steinberg-oriented undither filter.
.TP 5
.B l:Vf
Alias for lso_undither:Vfs.
.TP 5
.B lso_undither:Vlight
Use a light causal undithering variant designed for parallel decode.
.TP 5
.B l:Vl
Alias for lso_undither:Vlight.
.TP 5
.B selective_blur:threshold=24
Use selective 3x3 binomial blur.  The threshold is an RGB distance in the
range 0..441.
.TP 5
.B s:T24
Compact form of selective_blur:threshold=24.
.RE
.PP
Set \fBSIXEL_DEQUANTIZE_LSO_VARIANT\fP to fs or light to select the
default lso_undither variant. Set
\fBSIXEL_DEQUANTIZE_SELECTIVE_BLUR_THRESHOLD\fP to an integer from 0 through
441 to select the default selective_blur threshold. Explicit suboptions take
precedence over these defaults.
.TP 5
.B \-S
Specify similarity bias for dequantization.
The argument must be an integer between 0 and 1000.
The default value is 30.
.TP 5
.B \-s
Resize the decoded image so that the longer edge becomes SIZE pixels.
The aspect ratio is preserved.
.TP 5
.B \-e
Specify edge protection bias for dequantization.
The argument must be an integer between 0 and 1000.
The default value is 0.
.TP 5
.B \-D
Decode the SIXEL stream into an RGBA surface.
The alpha channel starts at zero so untouched pixels remain transparent.
.TP 5
.B \-= COUNT, \-\-threads=COUNT|auto
Override the decoder worker count.  Provide a positive integer COUNT to
keep deterministic band ordering while enabling multi-band parallelism.
Use "auto" to match the detected hardware thread count.
When SIXEL_THREADS is unset or empty, the sixel2png frontend defaults to
"auto".
.TP 5
.B \-G POLICY[:KEY=VALUE], \-\-gpu\-policy=POLICY[:KEY=VALUE]
Choose the decoder accelerator policy.  \fBoff\fP keeps the CPU path,
\fBauto\fP uses a supported GPU for sufficiently large images, and
\fBforce\fP requires GPU acceleration.
The decoder suboption \fB:dequant_threshold=PIXELS\fP, with short form
\fB:DPIXELS\fP, sets the minimum image size used by \fBauto\fP.
.TP 5
.B \-j POLICY[:KEY=VALUE], \-\-runtime\-policy=POLICY[:KEY=VALUE]
Choose process-wide runtime tuning. POLICY is \fBauto\fP,
\fBnone/scalar\fP, \fBsse2\fP, \fBavx\fP, or \fBneon\fP and limits the SIMD
implementation selected at runtime.
The decoder suboption \fB:parallel_skew=-20..20\fP, with short form
\fB:KVALUE\fP, biases decoder worker spans.
.TP 5
.B \-x MODE[:KEY=VALUE], \-\-diagnostics=MODE[:KEY=VALUE]
Choose diagnostic presentation. MODE is \fBhuman\fP (default) or
\fBcode\fP. Common suboptions are \fB:prefix_suggestions=0|1\fP
(\fB:P0|:P1\fP), \fB:fuzzy_suggestions=0|1\fP
(\fB:F0|:F1\fP), \fB:path_suggestions=0|1\fP
(\fB:S0|:S1\fP), and \fB:force_colors=0|1\fP
(\fB:C0|:C1\fP). \fB:trace_topic=LIST\fP
(\fB:TLIST\fP) selects a comma-separated topic list. Abort tracing uses
\fB:abort_trace=0|1\fP (\fB:A0|:A1\fP).
.TP 5
.B \-J PATH, \-\-log\-path=PATH
Write the shared JSON timeline log to PATH. This option takes precedence
over \fBSIXEL_LOG_PATH\fP.
.TP 5
.B \-% KEY=VALUE, \--env=KEY=VALUE
Set a process environment variable before decoding.
This option can be repeated.
.TP 5
.B \-V
Show version and license information, then exit.
.TP 5
.B \-H
Show usage information, then exit.


.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES"
\fIsixel2png\fP honours the following environment variables:
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DIAG_MODE
.br
select human or code diagnostics. Set to "code" to emit stable LSX*
diagnostic headers. The \fB\-x MODE\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OPTION_PREFIX_SUGGESTIONS
.br
toggle the prefix disambiguation hints emitted when a value matches more
than one option. Set to "1" (the default when unset) to print the
candidate list, or "0" to silence the diagnostic. Library embedders
must opt in explicitly. The \fB\-x *:prefix_suggestions=0|1\fP
suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OPTION_FUZZY_SUGGESTIONS
.br
toggle the normalized Levenshtein suggestions that recommend the closest
option names after a typo. Set to "1" (the default when unset) to print
the hint list, or "0" to disable it. Library embedders must opt in
explicitly. The \fB\-x *:fuzzy_suggestions=0|1\fP suboption takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_OPTION_PATH_SUGGESTIONS
.br
toggle the filesystem diagnostics that explain why a path could not be
resolved. Set to "1" to show the guidance, or "0" (the default) to suppress
it. The converter frontends keep the default disabled; library embedders must
opt in explicitly. The \fB\-x *:path_suggestions=0|1\fP suboption takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_STATUS_FORCE_COLORS
.br
force ANSI colorized diagnostics from status markup output. Set to "1" to
emit color sequences without relying on TTY detection. The
\fB\-x *:force_colors=0|1\fP suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_TRACE_TOPIC
.br
enable topic-scoped debug traces using comma-separated tokens. The
\fB\-x *:trace_topic=LIST\fP suboption (short form \fB:TLIST\fP) takes
precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_ABORT_TRACE
.br
dump abort backtraces when \fIsixel2png\fP terminates abnormally. Set to "0" to
disable or "1" to enable tracing. Unset, empty, or invalid values preserve the
enabled default. The \fB\-x *:abort_trace=0|1\fP suboption (short form
\fB:A0|:A1\fP) takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_LOG_PATH
.br
write the shared JSON timeline log when set. The
\fB\-J/\-\-log\-path\fP option takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_THREADS
.br
Override the decoder worker count using the same syntax as the
\-=/\-\-threads option.  Accepts positive integers or "auto" to match the
hardware thread count. Empty or unset values make sixel2png use "auto".
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_SIMD_LEVEL
.br
Limit SIMD selection to auto, none/scalar, sse2, avx, or neon.
The \fB\-j\fP runtime policy base takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_PARALLEL_SKEW
.br
Bias parallel decode spans by -20 through 20 percent. Defaults to 0.
The \fB\-j *:parallel_skew=VALUE\fP suboption
(short form \fB:KVALUE\fP) takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DEQUANTIZE_LSO_VARIANT
.br
Set the default lso_undither variant to fs or light. The dequantize
suboption takes precedence.
.TP 5
.B SIXEL_DEQUANTIZE_SELECTIVE_BLUR_THRESHOLD
.br
Set the default selective_blur RGB distance threshold to an integer from
0 through 441. The dequantize suboption takes precedence.


